1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,678
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,737 --> 00:00:09,987
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:09,987 --> 00:00:10,706
Let's begin!

4
00:00:11,766 --> 00:00:15,780
Welcome to Stage 9, Unit 1: Photosynthesis and Transport in Plants.

5
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,835
Deforestation is destroying forests full of life.

6
00:00:19,835 --> 00:00:25,407
Plants are producers: they make their own food by photosynthesis, which uses carbon dioxide.

7
00:00:25,407 --> 00:00:29,900
So how does cutting down trees affect us, besides reducing our food supply?

8
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:33,716
Plants make their own food by photosynthesis.

9
00:00:33,716 --> 00:00:39,767
They use energy from light to turn carbon dioxide from the air and water from the soil into glucose,

10
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:40,966
a sugar, and oxygen.

11
00:00:42,025 --> 00:00:46,159
We can summarise it with a word equation: carbon dioxide plus water,

12
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:50,233
in the presence of light and chlorophyll, makes glucose plus oxygen.

13
00:00:51,293 --> 00:00:55,248
'Photo' means from light, and 'synthesis' means putting together.

14
00:00:55,248 --> 00:00:59,681
The glucose lets plants form new cells and tissues, which we call biomass.

15
00:01:00,741 --> 00:01:03,377
Two pieces of pondweed are placed in water.

16
00:01:03,377 --> 00:01:09,847
One lamp is 10 centimetres away from the first beaker; another lamp is 50 centimetres away from the second.

17
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:14,401
Predict: which pondweed will give off more bubbles of gas? Pause and decide.

18
00:01:15,461 --> 00:01:18,936
Watch. Bubbles start to rise from both pieces of pondweed.

19
00:01:19,995 --> 00:01:26,466
The pondweed close to the lamp gives off about 40 bubbles a minute; the one far away gives off only about 6.

20
00:01:27,526 --> 00:01:31,720
Explain what you saw. The bubbles are oxygen, made by photosynthesis.

21
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:38,130
The closer lamp gives the pondweed more light energy, so it photosynthesises faster and makes more oxygen.

22
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:43,343
Light is needed for photosynthesis, and more light means a faster rate, up to a limit.

23
00:01:43,343 --> 00:01:45,679
Pause and explain it in your own words.

24
00:01:46,739 --> 00:01:53,210
A student counts the bubbles given off by pondweed in one minute, with the lamp at five different distances.

25
00:01:54,269 --> 00:02:00,680
At 10 centimetres there are 40 bubbles a minute. At 20 centimetres there are 26, and at 30 centimetres, 15.

26
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:07,432
The further away the lamp, the fewer the bubbles, but the line is a curve, not a straight line.

27
00:02:08,491 --> 00:02:11,607
Pause and decide: what is the independent variable,

28
00:02:11,607 --> 00:02:15,381
and why should the student keep the water temperature the same?

29
00:02:16,441 --> 00:02:22,313
Plants are well adapted for photosynthesis. Leaves have a large surface area to capture sunlight,

30
00:02:22,313 --> 00:02:25,608
and they're thin, so gases diffuse in and out quickly.

31
00:02:25,608 --> 00:02:30,760
Tiny openings called stomata, mostly on the underside of leaves, let gases in and out.

32
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:38,051
Photosynthesis happens in chloroplasts, which contain the green pigment chlorophyll that absorbs light.

33
00:02:38,051 --> 00:02:41,765
Root hairs give roots a huge surface area for absorbing water.

34
00:02:42,825 --> 00:02:47,319
Some oxygen is used for respiration; the rest escapes through the stomata.

35
00:02:47,319 --> 00:02:53,729
Glucose gives the plant energy, and extra glucose is stored as starch, in leaves, roots, stems and fruits.

36
00:02:53,729 --> 00:02:56,905
So the energy in every food chain comes from the Sun!

37
00:02:57,965 --> 00:03:01,799
If a leaf has photosynthesised, it contains starch. To test it,

38
00:03:01,799 --> 00:03:06,831
boil the leaf in water to stop all reactions, then in ethanol, heated in hot water,

39
00:03:06,831 --> 00:03:12,703
to remove the green chlorophyll. Careful: ethanol is flammable! Then soften the leaf in hot water.

40
00:03:13,763 --> 00:03:20,113
Add a few drops of iodine solution. Iodine is normally brown, but turns blue-black when starch is present.

41
00:03:21,173 --> 00:03:25,008
Keep a plant in the dark for 48 hours so it uses up its starch.

42
00:03:25,008 --> 00:03:29,381
Cover half a leaf with black paper and put the plant in bright sunlight.

43
00:03:29,381 --> 00:03:34,294
Only the uncovered half turns blue-black, showing that photosynthesis needs light.
